    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0453" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg379"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to the Marquis
                        de Montholon</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 7, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to enclose for your
                    information a copy of a communication of the 30th ultimo, from the War
                    Department, in regard to the case of the French merchant vessel Le Verrier,
                    which formed the subject of your note of the 30th of September, 1865.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, a renewed assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marquis de Montholon</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>








